  "conclusions": {
    "per_launch": "Per-launch overlap lowers wall time by about 3.60% versus single-buffer in this diagnostic window and does not increase wall-minus-GPU-span cost. However, concurrent command buffers inflate summed GPU busy time by about 68.18%, so contention consumes most of the overlap benefit. Candidate wall remains slightly above MLX wall; the >1.0 gate still fails. The exact GPU resource causing contention is not identified by these timestamps.",
